Subject: ACPI: do not install the PCI config default region handler without PCI

`acpi_gbl_default_address_spaces` names PCI config space unconditionally, but
`acpi_ev_install_space_handler` only compiles a case for it when
`ACPI_PCI_CONFIGURED` is defined, which follows `CONFIG_PCI`. On a kernel built
without PCI the loop therefore reaches the `default:` label, returns
`AE_BAD_PARAMETER`, and the whole namespace load fails:

    ACPI Error: AE_BAD_PARAMETER, During Region initialization
    ACPI: Unable to load the System Description Tables

Firecracker enumerates its virtio-mmio devices through ACPI and its published
guest configuration disables PCI, so a stock upstream kernel built with that
configuration cannot find its root device and panics. The condition is still
present in 6.12 LTS.

Keep the default space list and the handler switch in agreement.
--- a/include/acpi/acconfig.h
+++ b/include/acpi/acconfig.h
@@ -161,7 +161,11 @@
 /* Maximum space_ids for Operation Regions */
 
 #define ACPI_MAX_ADDRESS_SPACE          255
+#ifdef ACPI_PCI_CONFIGURED
 #define ACPI_NUM_DEFAULT_SPACES         4
+#else
+#define ACPI_NUM_DEFAULT_SPACES         3
+#endif
 
 /* Array sizes.  Used for range checking also */
 
--- a/drivers/acpi/acpica/evhandler.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/acpica/evhandler.c
@@ -26,7 +26,9 @@
 u8 acpi_gbl_default_address_spaces[ACPI_NUM_DEFAULT_SPACES] = {
 	ACPI_ADR_SPACE_SYSTEM_MEMORY,
 	ACPI_ADR_SPACE_SYSTEM_IO,
+#ifdef ACPI_PCI_CONFIGURED
 	ACPI_ADR_SPACE_PCI_CONFIG,
+#endif
 	ACPI_ADR_SPACE_DATA_TABLE
 };
 
